**1. `resolve` parameter (server directive)**

> "monitors changes of the IP addresses that correspond to a domain name of the server, and automatically modifies the upstream configuration without the need of restarting nginx (1.5.12). The server group must reside in the [shared memory](#zone). In order for this parameter to work, the `resolver` directive must be specified in the [http](ngx_http_core_module.html#resolver) block or in the corresponding [upstream](#resolver) block."
>
> "Prior to version 1.27.3, this parameter was available only as part of our [commercial subscription]."

So `resolve` is available in open source from **nginx 1.27.3**. Before that it was commercial-only.

**2. `keepalive` directive**

> "Enables or disables caching of keepalive connections to upstream servers. Since 1.29.7, by default the cache for connections is activated and these connections are not [shared](#keepalive_local) between different [locations]."

> "For HTTP, the [proxy_http_version] directive should be “`1.1`” (by default since 1.29.7) or set to “`2`” and the “Connection” header field should be cleared. This example is for versions prior to 1.29.7:"

```nginx
upstream http_backend {
    server 127.0.0.1:8080;
    keepalive 16;
}

server {
    location /http/ {
        proxy_pass http://http_backend;
        # proxy_http_version 1.1;          # before version 1.29.7
        # proxy_set_header Connection "";  # before version 1.29.7
    }
}
```

**3. `keepalive_timeout` default**

> "Default: `keepalive_timeout 60s;`"
>
> "Sets a timeout during which an idle keepalive connection to an upstream server will stay open."

It was introduced in version 1.15.3.

**4. `zone` requirement for `resolve`**

The `resolve` parameter requires the server group to reside in shared memory: "The server group must reside in the shared memory." The `zone` directive provides this:

> "Defines the `name` and `size` of the shared memory zone that keeps the group's configuration and run-time state that are shared between worker processes."

Example from the page:

```nginx
resolver 10.0.0.1;

upstream dynamic {
    zone upstream_dynamic 64k;
    server backend3.example.com resolve;
}
```

Note that the page's `zone` directive itself is not marked commercial. The commercial part is changing group membership through the API without restarting nginx.

